---
import NewsletterTools from '../components/NewsletterTools.astro';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { getStories } from '../lib/feeds';
import { withStory } from '../lib/omg';
import { goodNews, shoutouts } from '../lib/community';
const { stories } = await getStories();
const all = withStory(stories);
// Lead = first take that has a photo, else the first take.
const lead = all.find((r) => r.image) ?? all[0];
const rest = all.filter((r) => r !== lead);
const tag = Astro.url.searchParams.get('tag');
---
<Layout title="OMG!" current="OMG!">
  <section class="page">
    {(tag === 'Good News' || tag === 'Shout-Outs') && <>
      <div class="pagehead"><h2>{tag}</h2><span>{tag === 'Good News' ? 'Upbeat stories from around Austin' : 'Birthdays, congrats and thank-yous'}</span></div>
      <div class="omgcols">
        <div class="posts">
          {tag === 'Good News' && goodNews.map((g) => (<article class="post"><div class="kicker">Good News · Sample</div><h3>{g.head}</h3><p>{g.blurb}</p></article>))}
          {tag === 'Shout-Outs' && shoutouts.map((g) => (<article class="post"><div class="kicker">{g.kind}{(g as any).real ? '' : ' · Sample'}</div><h3>{g.who}</h3><p>{g.note}</p></article>))}
        </div>
        <aside class="omgside">
          <div class="sendbox"><b>Got one to share?</b> {tag === 'Good News' ? 'Tell us the good news happening in your corner of Austin.' : 'Birthdays, congrats, thank-yous and anniversaries.'} <a href="/contact">Send it in →</a></div>
          <NewsletterTools />
          <div class="sponsor"><div class="label">Advertise</div><b>Reach Austin readers</b>Want your business here? <a href="/contact">Get in touch →</a></div>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </>}
    {tag && tag !== 'Good News' && tag !== 'Shout-Outs' && <><p class="kicker">{tag}</p><p>Reactions for this one are coming soon. <a href="/omg">See everything</a>.</p></>}
    {!tag && <>
    <div class="pagehead"><h2>OMG!</h2><span>Austin news, with a side eye.</span></div>
    <div class="omgcols"><div>
    {all.map((r) => (
      <article class="take">
        {r.label && <div class="kicker">{r.label}</div>}
        <div class="hd">{r.head}</div>
        <p class="bigline"><em>OMG!</em> {r.line}</p>
        {r.link && <a href={r.link} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the story →</a>}
      </article>
    ))}
    <article class="post mtm" id="mtm">
      <div class="kicker">From the family · Mind the Marbles newsletter</div>
      <h3>I Got a Text Monday. It&rsquo;s Thursday.</h3>
      <p class="mtmsub">It was a three-word question.<br />Now the answer needs an apology.</p>
      <p>How long can you leave a text sitting there before it becomes a whole thing?</p>
      <p>I&rsquo;ll tell you. Three days.</p>
      <p>A friend texted me Monday: &ldquo;You coming Saturday?&rdquo; That&rsquo;s it. The answer is &ldquo;yes.&rdquo;</p>
      <p>I read it Monday. I thought, I&rsquo;ll answer when I have a minute.</p>
      <p>Tuesday, I opened it to answer, and then I started thinking about the right way to answer. Wednesday, a plain &ldquo;yes&rdquo; felt rude after all this time, so I started typing &ldquo;Sorry for the late reply!&rdquo;</p>
      <p>By Thursday, my reply was a paragraph. The question was &ldquo;You coming Saturday?&rdquo;</p>
      <p>It had gone from &ldquo;Yes&rdquo; to &ldquo;Before I answer, I&rsquo;d like to address the events of this week.&rdquo;</p>
      <p>I&rsquo;ve now read his text so many times I could recite it. I still haven&rsquo;t replied.</p>
      <p>He&rsquo;s not even mad. I&rsquo;ve been mad for both of us.</p>
      <h4 class="mtmh">The Recognition</h4>
      <p>Sometimes the longer you wait, the bigger the reply gets.</p>
      <p>Not because you don&rsquo;t care about them. Not because you&rsquo;re rude.</p>
      <p>Because your mind thinks: &ldquo;If I answer now, I have to explain why it took this long.&rdquo;</p>
      <p>The text was never hard. The guilt piled on top of it got hard. Every day you wait, the reply gets heavier.</p>
      <p>Time to reply: two seconds.<br />Time spent not replying: three days.</p>
      <p>You didn&rsquo;t ignore the text. You just kept adding to it.</p>
      <h4 class="mtmh">Remember This</h4>
      <p class="mtmbox">Sometimes you&rsquo;re not avoiding the reply. You&rsquo;re avoiding the fact that you haven&rsquo;t replied.</p>
      <p>And honestly? &ldquo;Sorry, been a week. Yes.&rdquo; is a complete text.</p>
      <h4 class="mtmh">Try This</h4>
      <p>The next time a text is sitting there, ask: <b>What&rsquo;s the shortest true answer?</b></p>
      <p>Not &ldquo;How do I explain the delay?&rdquo; Not &ldquo;What&rsquo;s the perfect way to say it?&rdquo; Not &ldquo;Do I need to apologize first?&rdquo;</p>
      <p>Then send that. It&rsquo;s a whole answer.</p>
      <h4 class="mtmh">Until next time, remember&hellip;</h4>
      <p>A late reply isn&rsquo;t a bad reply.<br />You&rsquo;re allowed to answer like a person.</p>
      <p><i>See you next week.</i> &mdash; <b>MIND THE MARBLES</b></p>
    </article>
    </div>
    <aside class="omgside">
      <div class="sendbox"><b>Good news? Birthday shout-out?</b> Share it with Austin. <a href="/contact">Send it in →</a></div>
      <NewsletterTools />
      <div class="sponsor"><div class="label">From the family</div><b>Mind the Marbles</b><em class="mtmjoke">&ldquo;I got a text Monday. It&rsquo;s Thursday.&rdquo;</em> This week&rsquo;s Mind the Marbles issue. <a href="#mtm">Read it below &darr;</a><br /><a class="cta" href="https://www.instagram.com/mindthemarbles/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Follow on Instagram →</a></div>
    </aside>
    </div>
  </>}
  </section>
</Layout>
